/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467600} {:answer/id #uuid "bdbfb014-4e69-5922-98b2-654a079851f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdbfb014-4e69-5922-98b2-654a079851f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467601} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebca5b66-72d2-5051-b663-b25f725bdc65" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "632c55e7-35c1-5a02-8973-af67647c4724" :question/math-academy-id "q-48018" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={log}_{2}⁡(x-2)?$  \n- **I.** $[-1,1]$\n- **II.** $[2,3)$\n- **III.** $[3,4]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $y={log}_{2}⁡(x-2)$ is not defined anywhere in this interval. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[2,3)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[3,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[3,4].$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f46a85-bb8a-511d-ad66-524153b56e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467602} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac808f8-b76f-5da9-9c2c-f50846ef33e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac808f8-b76f-5da9-9c2c-f50846ef33e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467603} :answer-field/id #uuid "69cd4ca1-53f7-5c26-b39d-e11af89e4852" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "867861da-42a3-56d6-b2be-e893dd3a6ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467604} {:answer/id #uuid "7d560fb8-d782-59c3-979e-b88c6fc64bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "867861da-42a3-56d6-b2be-e893dd3a6ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467604} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce979cb4-0614-53e2-8a28-d665b639c546" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468523} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cd7cb5-c364-5a3f-b04d-9d888c1844c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467606} {:answer/id #uuid "10f5285e-8e1a-55c5-9d7e-e0ce7e671593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28cd7cb5-c364-5a3f-b04d-9d888c1844c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467606} :answer-field/id #uuid "a62ebe16-a0c0-5d34-b75e-fc7858ec905c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85a69bc3-3237-5b5c-9f6c-9b2553833eb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-48020" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)^{2}?$ \n- **I.** $[-1,0]$\n- **II.** $(-2,1]$\n- **III.** $[-3,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,0]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-1,0]$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-2,1]$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-3,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)^{2}$ is not defined at $x=-2.$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "485fd759-96b3-553f-9eaa-849878c30885" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Jump Discontinuity Given a Function Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9ffb34-162b-5145-9c40-101a442547a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467608} {:answer/id #uuid "838c1862-e33f-5469-8aaf-7e17990df69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838c1862-e33f-5469-8aaf-7e17990df69c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467609} :answer-field/id #uuid "405153bc-6d67-54bd-bd2b-59adea706ce6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468525} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573f4b42-cfcf-56d0-9467-f208cd5625a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467610} {:answer/id #uuid "ca467abb-57ef-5f98-bf7e-6827a342e71b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "573f4b42-cfcf-56d0-9467-f208cd5625a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467610} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a64fe7e-2eab-5f3d-93d7-58160ec21920" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468526} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88b5c6f6-a2d2-5656-a44f-935d42e30104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467612} {:answer/id #uuid "25356ae2-6276-56b3-8a7d-fffb7a272e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b5c6f6-a2d2-5656-a44f-935d42e30104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467612} :answer-field/id #uuid "016967b9-4c97-5a30-856e-0c57b4dbf834" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93ca2ad1-e9ee-58b8-96fe-892745e095e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-48167" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x)$ below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3, & x<1 \\\\ 1-{x}^{3}, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- **II.** It has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$\n- **III.** It's continuous at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "For $x=1,$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(1)=1-{1}^{3}=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{2}+3)=({1}^{2}+3)=4\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(1-{x}^{3})=(1-{1}^{3})=0.\n$$\n\nSo both the left and right limits exist and are finite, but they are not equal. $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$\n\nHence, I is true, while II and III are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d01d143-68f2-534a-8be6-4f63f9ab0d40" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement On the Intermediate Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1030b649-2e0a-51bb-8114-4235e6e28e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327076} {:answer/id #uuid "113a49d2-c59a-55ba-8ee0-5f66c8da879a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III, II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327085} {:answer/id #uuid "13937bf8-316a-57ee-965e-b8c35314ac95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327102} {:answer/id #uuid "3594121f-cd76-5a51-8a9d-372b486a97bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II, I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327402} {:answer/id #uuid "4e3edb4d-31e5-5a5f-bd10-40503be98128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1030b649-2e0a-51bb-8114-4235e6e28e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327076} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c09edd3-38cc-54ac-aac2-51bbb42a21c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74f6e633-2570-5d1a-abe0-fed2503f6040" :question/math-academy-id "q-48430" :question/problem "A statement of the intermediate value theorem is given below but some of its parts are missing.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is $\\text{ ______ }$ on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $\\text{ _________ }$, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nGoing from left to right, in which order should the parts I-III, listed below, be placed into the blank spaces to complete the statement of the theorem?\n\nI. continuous\n\nII. $f(a)$ and $f(b)$ inclusively\n\nIII. defined" :question/worked-solution "The intermediate value theorem states the following.\n\n*Let $f(x)$ be a function that is **continuous** on a closed interval $[a,b].$ If $k$ is a number that lies between $f(a)$ **and** $f(b)$ **inclusively**, then there exists a number $c\\in [a,b]$ such that $f(c)=k.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f17851-b5f1-5589-89e5-4642a8d2d249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467614} {:answer/id #uuid "fe31214d-0432-50de-9cd1-6ad24b62b595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f17851-b5f1-5589-89e5-4642a8d2d249" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467614} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1af9b0a-7ec1-5f15-ab7a-56fa74b6fabe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468528} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd93754f-1a73-5ffe-8b5e-62295879212b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467616} {:answer/id #uuid "97f0f22d-a1ec-5f03-b20b-292b7ce3521b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97f0f22d-a1ec-5f03-b20b-292b7ce3521b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467617} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ff5b55-724a-5d7c-a019-33906583195b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bf0a3fa-7f7c-5c54-a84c-1a06af8969ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467618} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed441dd-6085-55e5-843b-f0100f281f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bf0a3fa-7f7c-5c54-a84c-1a06af8969ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467618} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bb492ea-182c-5f4c-80ed-d7362312d50e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468530}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "12754a03-432b-5bc6-9c26-008364483fd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48497" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4]?$\n- **I.** $g(x)=|x-1|$\n- **II.** $f(x)={x}^{4}$\n- **III.** $h(x)=\\sqrt{x-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4],$ the function must be continuous on $[0,4]$ and differentiable on $(0,4).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $g(x)=|x-1|$ is continuous on $[0,4]$ but has a corner at $x=1.$ Hence, it is not differentiable at $x=1,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(0,4).$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $f(x)={x}^{4}$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[0,4]$ and differentiable on $(0,4).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function  $h(x)=\\sqrt{x-1}$ is not defined on $(-\\infty ,1).$ Hence, it is not continuous on $[0,4].$ Therefore, $h(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only function II satisfies the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[0,4].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc7d5d6-a451-5962-afc9-9fff555f20ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467620} {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80618245-4ae0-5579-a15a-1159b6d87793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467621} :answer-field/id #uuid "2697fbf1-11b6-59e7-a243-ede0e967f0fe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467622} {:answer/id #uuid "250ef74c-ffc2-556d-a0a3-798c3e88030d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f9f4c1-1b21-59f3-8a3f-07dc9f40bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467622} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8df5920-44fd-5cbe-9f0a-2111cda02c34" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} {:answer/id #uuid "762ae4d9-bf4c-5ca6-bb90-84a859083154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5889732e-c51e-5840-9f31-81e7f3e6b2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2facf3b-7a9b-53cc-9a3f-b2a9bf7a9c24" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "101d0c36-a705-552a-b14b-442022f64eda" :question/math-academy-id "q-48734" :question/problem "![](images/14/14fdc374842064ad40ebbadf3dab16191ecfdeec8c416b4e7f17beffce44fb40.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=3$\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=3$\n- $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=3.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(3)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement II is false. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the derivative is undefined at $x=3$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function does not have a local maximum at $x=3$ since $f(3)\\le f(x)$ for $x$ close enough  to the point $x=3,$ so,  actually,  $f(x)$ has local minimum at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e1f3def-98d2-524a-b778-f7e66a7f3296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467626} {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1a3726-de03-5ff7-9514-9c9aa55b2a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467627} :answer-field/id #uuid "86fbad27-f24f-5ab5-9dc2-2649e548b79d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "956e3925-042a-5383-b9cd-d81e8467a088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467628} {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906240b1-a7be-5057-81ba-1361d1041439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467629} :answer-field/id #uuid "98dade12-9621-5587-bfac-2f8ef6ab2b14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b46b1cc-def4-5734-bd89-8f1d5131c333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467630} {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1649fad-0b66-52f0-b7d5-6860409aa309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467631} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4e72066-eadb-5611-801e-ce8cccffd34f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5dfd5ad-23a9-54fc-83bf-a64cab147aed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48737" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a2298a8255a86c803560793658593a22f7f77590ef350c1e0cebd974fce7750.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. $f(x)$ has  a stationary point at $x=0$\n\nII. $f(x)$ has  a local maximum at $x=2$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case,  the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a local maximum at $x=2$ since $f(2)\\ge f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a sharp edge (corner) at $x=2$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(2)$ does not exist. Hence, $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, all statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083303 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1894719c-d398-515d-9a7b-6af74727106c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Improper Integrals of the Second Kind"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d097d65c-ca38-51c7-902f-ceb12ecc4778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467632} {:answer/id #uuid "226a6a50-79b8-5c33-985c-5f775a2757c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "226a6a50-79b8-5c33-985c-5f775a2757c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467633} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b100ce3-ba13-57fa-adb1-8b97906c346c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e91f9305-12b5-5f9a-ad08-1a546a489375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467634} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7cb5b3-dae8-51b6-9737-7ea6e66b57d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e91f9305-12b5-5f9a-ad08-1a546a489375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467634} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf5b4d8f-0e7c-5a34-9eec-fe772d51d84c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e4352e-1743-545b-8868-832df848687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467636} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0cc153-5d01-50ab-9bb3-8a9f885d2be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e4352e-1743-545b-8868-832df848687e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467636} :answer-field/id #uuid "24371f23-5748-56a3-bf21-04ee080c6fc5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67f5d543-d28a-5536-ab0c-6f8fec51324b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49928" :question/problem "Which of the following is an improper integral of the second kind?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}-9}\\,$\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-4}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}-9}\\,$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given integrals.\n\n- Integral I is an improper integral of the second kind since it has finite limits, and \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-9}\\to -\\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {3}^{-}.\n$$\n\n- Integral II is an improper integral over an *infinite* domain since its lower limit is infinite.\n\n- Integral III is not an improper integral since it has finite limits and the function under the integral is finite at every point $x\\in [1,3].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd82d96b-34d5-5d20-b810-7ea88b0b5797" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Stationary Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} {:answer/id #uuid "613a05d1-be2e-50ec-a143-b9bd92523dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1400080f-29b9-5c0b-8fff-a02b1e3db551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467638} :answer-field/id #uuid "936bcfa4-d2d6-56bc-951a-d3fb63ec7798" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} {:answer/id #uuid "de6a0b4d-d5db-57b2-b79f-fc23d0c4a768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a5309f7-7b7d-5141-8adf-5fd91dcf5b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467640} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a065266-b7e5-54c1-b994-892844b67807" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} {:answer/id #uuid "3503fafc-99d4-55a2-8b84-ae4563b1ad39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b3cbfb6-b114-5d0c-bde7-abe9838a454d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467642} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbaebdb6-1441-5c65-a2f2-c74e1d11eb4f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "009c7b44-827f-54c3-aa43-59cb0c58cb71" :question/math-academy-id "q-50143" :question/problem "![](images/50/50472b92dc5fbcc8688bb1d5459f910fb2d3f3c0ee564ba671cb6a53ce8df721.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$\n- ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e3/e328914d55b82fdd07147f683aa44aebbc3f3e908f180e6632332119c81ce482.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the slopes of the slope field are horizontal along the line $y=-1,$ as shown above. Therefore, the right-hand side of the differential equation should evaluate to zero on this line. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each equation:\n\n- Equation I does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}={e}^{y+1}$ is never zero.\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x(y+1)$ evaluates to zero at $x=0$ and $y=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172016 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3e3fdc8-67d0-5b46-9c6b-c1ec8d4ea24f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation That Generates a Slope Field Using Asymptotes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c66c442f-84ec-5b88-bd98-fd9efdff281b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467644} {:answer/id #uuid "aae2582a-0183-57ed-bc6c-e0fad39e48b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aae2582a-0183-57ed-bc6c-e0fad39e48b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467645} :answer-field/id #uuid "4014543f-2bdb-54cd-b8d4-a799fdbe3913" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58199bae-a5df-50bb-898b-cb09f6da04f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467646} {:answer/id #uuid "edd3e05c-30a9-5909-ad89-48705f604f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58199bae-a5df-50bb-898b-cb09f6da04f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467646} :answer-field/id #uuid "910c1975-2d45-5166-b546-9cc56824291c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb59070-29c0-590f-a938-6111ddb1d321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467648} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddd639c-9761-51b1-bb4e-04dcdf95e6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb59070-29c0-590f-a938-6111ddb1d321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467648} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2598018-4757-537b-839c-45823c668a17" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61e999bc-d48d-5bd0-9909-d28a8b568c3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-50349" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a64064f114ac2e6acafa791c4fda50849cad6f3387c4793bdf991c95ae8e542.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$\n- ${y}^{′}=x+y$\n- ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "![](images/6a/6a119b24c773a25bf3530dbfb8574c710cc37a5e970d92112aee5f489551ef02.png)\n\n \n\nNotice the following properties of the given slope field:\n\n- The slopes of the slope field become horizontal at $x=0.$\n\n- For $x\\ne 0,$ the slopes of the slope field become vertical as $y\\to -1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each equation.\n\n- Equation I gives the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y+1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ and for $x\\ne 0,$ we have \n\n$$\n|{y}^{′}|=|\\frac{x}{y+1}|\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=x+y$ does not evaluate to zero on $x=0$ (the value depends on $y$).\n\n- Equation III does *not* give the required behavior. The right-hand side of ${y}^{′}=\\frac{x}{y-1}$ evaluates to zero on $x=0,$ but for $x\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=|\\frac{x}{y-1}|\\to \\frac{|x|}{2}\\,\\text{as}\\,y\\to -1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7434f6cd-5abd-5918-983c-90f901173537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467650} {:answer/id #uuid "390198b7-c54f-5cd9-9c6c-20eb14f25176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "390198b7-c54f-5cd9-9c6c-20eb14f25176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467651} :answer-field/id #uuid "9223a194-f14e-5bca-a4c3-a9be1301213f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8c9699-34bd-5a5b-b1d1-7fc0cd00c967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467652} {:answer/id #uuid "32c64784-f8cf-5e6a-8345-7313e29025cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8c9699-34bd-5a5b-b1d1-7fc0cd00c967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467652} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec5739d-20d1-54f9-9ab8-3fc8589202be" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0e3c250-5a95-5d66-9b29-c6400da6d824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467654} {:answer/id #uuid "c5386d8a-3465-59f6-895b-f357aefa1a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5386d8a-3465-59f6-895b-f357aefa1a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467655} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f75b307-815b-51f7-b01e-ead1c5a03e0b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29977f9f-fbdd-580d-914b-4f20cb78cbe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-50506" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n- **I.** ${\\sum }_{n=5}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$\n- **II.** ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(2)}^{n}$\n- **III.** ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{8}^{n+1}}{{16}^{n-1}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=5}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ starts with $n=5.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{6}}{{a}_{5}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{6}}{\\frac{1}{2}{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{(2)}^{n}$ starts with $n=1.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{8{(2)}^{2}}{8{(2)}^{1}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- The series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{8}^{n+1}}{{16}^{n-1}}$ starts with $n=0.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{{a}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\frac{{8}^{1+1}}{{16}^{1-1}}}{\\frac{{8}^{0+1}}{{16}^{0-1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{{16}^{0}})}{(\\frac{{8}^{1}}{{16}^{-1}})} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{{16}^{0}})(\\frac{{16}^{-1}}{{8}^{1}}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{8}^{2}}{1})(\\frac{1}{16\\cdot 8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series  I and III converge."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subsets of Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce3b13c-fb26-5cdb-823b-ca12d87dcc29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467656} {:answer/id #uuid "4d99d91e-efdd-5a22-8ce6-9d8df760800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d99d91e-efdd-5a22-8ce6-9d8df760800e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467657} :answer-field/id #uuid "37f9faab-1148-50bf-98d5-9657cccc6502" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468549} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a35154f-b61f-507c-a4f8-90c4cf4d5c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467658} {:answer/id #uuid "9488a339-5ba0-54e0-82a1-c0571ea80c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9488a339-5ba0-54e0-82a1-c0571ea80c0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467659} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9e8c14-b0a7-5878-a123-15208210b57a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40a1b98-03b0-592f-9753-c93046815294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467660} {:answer/id #uuid "c964f3a3-9c86-5204-9476-a17284a88218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c964f3a3-9c86-5204-9476-a17284a88218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467661} :answer-field/id #uuid "3695a8e5-9f68-5a86-83e9-3b39972d0070" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe2b18ec-0853-5e8f-951d-8609485c9093" :question/math-academy-id "q-506" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n- **I.** ${Q}^{+}$ (the set of positive rationals)\n- **II.** ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- **III.** $N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every positive rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every negative integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4316287-e6f4-5c71-8743-249965e93785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467662} {:answer/id #uuid "0d5b25f2-ad9a-5e2f-a467-62aebcb4c800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d5b25f2-ad9a-5e2f-a467-62aebcb4c800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467663} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc30e13-6c4c-51bf-9649-4940879f0a6e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15239395-17ec-5d90-8ed6-dae47a5b516c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467664} {:answer/id #uuid "b9279de7-3faf-547d-b961-fdffdf72f3a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15239395-17ec-5d90-8ed6-dae47a5b516c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467664} :answer-field/id #uuid "73db372a-04b8-52e1-b15d-153eaeca8010" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812e2132-8055-538a-81b4-e7b919fdc93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467666} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf07043-0394-579e-9adb-f5a8794e6ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "812e2132-8055-538a-81b4-e7b919fdc93a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467666} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f7b7695-a3ac-5b03-bf35-127476bb6ba2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3027786-58ab-53d9-9e13-106f7ec40b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-50871" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=0.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=1$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=4$\n- **III.** The series diverges at $x=-2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=0,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[0,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[0,4).$\n\n![](images/a5/a56e24009403f0177f608ba932c03ab77e8db35e1db3e1221c4fb49efca7219f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $1\\in [0,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $4\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-2\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332834 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7c7875c-fb08-5fb9-95a6-6d4c334d3a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467668} {:answer/id #uuid "b7697c61-e32a-5449-a404-f95821b2faf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7697c61-e32a-5449-a404-f95821b2faf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467669} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c9d32b0-1a92-5c27-a611-84659667e826" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468555} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79ed778-e03d-5a13-8aec-70d926886135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467670} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1c2fe6-7bc4-59a9-bd46-db90d677cd88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a79ed778-e03d-5a13-8aec-70d926886135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467670} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb45d0e8-95af-5941-8c8e-1df1bc25a55b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468556} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a555f3f3-d734-5304-a0c7-3e541caad244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467672} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5d1cf7-3b8c-5cea-9259-b41ba8e81d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a555f3f3-d734-5304-a0c7-3e541caad244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467672} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c1626a0-6ea2-5f94-b208-8c642c9defd1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2ee1b3ae-f8d2-59d0-abf6-79ccfd75cdf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-50873" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x+2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=-3$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $1,$ i.e., $R\\ge 1.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-3,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-3,-1].$\n\n![](images/93/93ab98aaa7170e5fcef1c090555f259b2030384b6f2f25a282af9d8b6a406ed2.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\in (-3,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-3\\notin (-3,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-\\frac{7}{2}\\notin (-3,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de8e2cbd-2cca-54d4-b53f-11f1742375a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467674} {:answer/id #uuid "90b8c826-ab66-5fe6-9c26-b504e31cd6f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de8e2cbd-2cca-54d4-b53f-11f1742375a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467674} :answer-field/id #uuid "47abf491-3b18-517c-9432-1a77835f69ff" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c34fdd9-c7d9-5163-8736-d94a57295338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467676} {:answer/id #uuid "228345a5-b436-5fd3-a6b7-477115126239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c34fdd9-c7d9-5163-8736-d94a57295338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467676} :answer-field/id #uuid "79210059-fe37-5b42-ab4d-9e06d408f996" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "603bd9ba-8227-5cfc-ac24-42a89368dbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467678} {:answer/id #uuid "67e22114-28c1-5927-9bf5-6eb1a2a135d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e22114-28c1-5927-9bf5-6eb1a2a135d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467679} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd62b1b3-17ad-588c-b5d5-c422db62c7ea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29a54ff7-5783-54c7-b610-5c600dd04d48" :question/math-academy-id "q-50874" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-4,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series diverges at $x=-5$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=2$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-4,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-4,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-4,2).$ \n\n![](images/a2/a246a6460d15037b469072b4275e51ff4dd9c56242f6ffeae1bebc2adf66f39f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $2\\notin [-4,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $-3\\in [-4,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2300bae0-298d-53b8-ab0d-12d87ac46d5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467680} {:answer/id #uuid "36bc1938-4be5-5a3d-aa29-252dd524ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36bc1938-4be5-5a3d-aa29-252dd524ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467681} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceabd937-f087-5722-8c9a-d4dbf4d0f9b4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e39a0cb-6e4d-56d5-a23c-41c3a5e61762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467682} {:answer/id #uuid "0b2ffdc0-c8c8-569e-89da-2c6ea8c2aea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e39a0cb-6e4d-56d5-a23c-41c3a5e61762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467682} :answer-field/id #uuid "9426409a-ac6f-506c-98a7-5f83162b0a11" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf5703cc-2efe-559c-9fb5-ff676ba60b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467684} {:answer/id #uuid "04771c22-bce4-501c-a4b9-4f52d83ab3ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf5703cc-2efe-559c-9fb5-ff676ba60b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467684} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bfba346-6758-55bf-9798-0053f1e86ced" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32c4dcc9-1fba-5e61-8a0a-ad46399f9d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-50876" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+1)^{n}$ converges at  $x=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-1,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{5}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{5}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}].$\n\n![](images/57/57208948dece1112674d3578763bc8d6b73d1d6ab91d160b14839e16a39cf2f6.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $-3\\in (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{7}{2}\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin (-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f76e57a-1ca0-528a-83d8-a658b709ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467686} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd70b0d-74ff-575c-9f41-331c8052230a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f76e57a-1ca0-528a-83d8-a658b709ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467686} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9f46eb-7d8b-5c31-85be-40e5cad1c55e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468564} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5888bd7f-0417-52e2-9a92-7c880ec24bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467688} {:answer/id #uuid "b848d96c-e2cc-5b77-b15f-3560a9b4590d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5888bd7f-0417-52e2-9a92-7c880ec24bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab3783e8-f88d-556b-acd1-93c5cd956bca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e011cc9-db9e-52c4-9b70-2cc44c5f65c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467690} {:answer/id #uuid "7816688d-7881-5671-bc85-e7a63dbf447a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e011cc9-db9e-52c4-9b70-2cc44c5f65c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467690} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccae151c-97cd-5e93-9baa-a5d477ca5334" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0bcb862b-db75-545a-8402-c194bc3da35a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50877" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-2.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-3$\n- **II.** The series diverges at $x=1$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=8$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $5,$ i.e., $R\\ge 5.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-2,8).$\n\n![](images/38/38763aa0d87065a01ccdf0d94bca2a4e1d6ef227aeab4aaacb9703246eee6abf.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-3\\notin [-2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-3.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $1\\in [-2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $8\\notin [-2,8),$  we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements must be true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6e5e228-fa65-531d-a8da-e444079bd9d8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Series Using Multiple Convergence Tests"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "624b7117-00f8-551a-809e-5d1c3ff1debc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467692} {:answer/id #uuid "a1161ac7-f2a2-58a6-8a07-6b82fbac85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1161ac7-f2a2-58a6-8a07-6b82fbac85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467693} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b52ba51-dd6a-5109-ad4a-86c7ab07785f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468567} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a95e3e6-c21e-5dba-88b4-2aa448e29ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467694} {:answer/id #uuid "c80a45eb-af40-56af-be7f-df024e54b91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a95e3e6-c21e-5dba-88b4-2aa448e29ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467694} :answer-field/id #uuid "640dfa81-f2e1-5fca-a3e6-abf23e497d33" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52924de1-0701-5aac-9b3a-e34d33354697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467696} {:answer/id #uuid "dde7684e-a4ef-50e4-a409-ed9aeefc8f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52924de1-0701-5aac-9b3a-e34d33354697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467696} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a21870-3114-52a9-bdfe-348f688b5b7a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a500c68-ffb3-5162-a19f-22fd0f314af1" :question/math-academy-id "q-50971" :question/problem "Which of the following series converge?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}$\n\nIII. ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We use the flowchart below to determine which tests to use for each series.\n\n![](images/3a/3aa7f0243efeab51d00aa9694dd018245f7ca4664cc1a5fdf4e646aebb61536e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's test each series in turn.\n\n- For the first series, we use the alternating series test. Observe that \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n!}\n$$\n\nis positive and decreasing for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, by the alternating series test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n!}\n$$\n\nis also convergent.\n\n- For the second series, we use the limit comparison test. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nWorking out the necessary limit, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{b}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}÷\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\\cdot \\sqrt{n}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2n}{n+2}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2}{(1+\\frac{2}{n})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1+0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $L=2$ is positive and finite. Now, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nis divergent by the $p$-series test. So, the series \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2\\sqrt{n}}{n+2}\n$$\n\nis also divergent by the limit comparison test.\n\n- For the final series, we use the $n$th term test for divergence. Let \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThen, we have ${lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=\\infty ,$ since the polynomial in the numerator grows faster than the polynomial in the denominator. Therefore, by the $n$th term test, the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{n}^{3}}{n+2{n}^{2}}\n$$\n\nis divergent.\n\nIn conclusion, only series I converges."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5633afc7-e223-5130-9090-0d9865542257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467698} {:answer/id #uuid "8be09054-e939-5cc8-b92f-f214cfcf82fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be09054-e939-5cc8-b92f-f214cfcf82fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467699} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1f48bc-fb36-5f83-8aa7-46fb5cb2d82e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d41b96c3-cfe1-58c9-a62b-16aa45f88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467700} {:answer/id #uuid "87a1ad38-a41b-5686-a7ca-5d675ff2cf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d41b96c3-cfe1-58c9-a62b-16aa45f88ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467700} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d22340-4fa0-5014-8865-2d0be6f7f86d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ed64b73-5791-59b1-83e8-1e3d847f7927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467702} {:answer/id #uuid "d539c28a-0e2c-5ae6-8fef-98fd25e1625a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ed64b73-5791-59b1-83e8-1e3d847f7927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467702} :answer-field/id #uuid "0523546d-7928-515a-b054-7e46e591c14b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc8d31c1-2a52-5465-9bb5-91b8bdc2abf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-51070" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5eae80c03e35f79eaa484a5d54f7fa1a0ec46a5f27480fb69089efab938eba06.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true. The graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking the pencil off the paper.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $f(x)$ has a cusp at this point and so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- Statement III is false. From the graph we can see that $f(x)$ has a corner point at $x=-1$ and so it is not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147430 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Simple Harmonic Motion Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c1f2c3b-1d34-5c06-b61c-46d1903e5e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467704} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dcd9f-31c4-523b-8ddc-4637dfa9e777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7dcd9f-31c4-523b-8ddc-4637dfa9e777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467705} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb0f775-1530-52d1-b49f-df3b6017042f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468573} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1598357d-613f-5fc5-8ce1-55e7dc1b98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467706} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0b795c-450c-5317-b8c4-dcb8c540442b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1598357d-613f-5fc5-8ce1-55e7dc1b98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467706} :answer-field/id #uuid "38477ec7-e808-5dbf-9eda-11186731007f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ab47045-d431-52de-91f8-aac2544bdf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467708} {:answer/id #uuid "099ed570-a048-5749-af1f-b679324dbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "099ed570-a048-5749-af1f-b679324dbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467709} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f979ad1-f9a7-5092-b7cc-ebe822b551bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "347ed2fe-a388-536f-85e7-6e55844b3b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-64252" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n- **I.** $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n- **II.** $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n- **III.** $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=81\\,⟹\\,\\omega =9.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9t$\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III could be used to represent $y(t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e735dc0-c691-579e-b252-edb026eeb71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467710} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d75e2e-d6bc-57ec-ae37-c69815c776ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1d75e2e-d6bc-57ec-ae37-c69815c776ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467711} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c70e2c6-e1e0-5572-9a05-ea0878c65ffa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a16d1d62-6621-503c-b0f9-bb715a8e1719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467712} {:answer/id #uuid "8440d621-4497-5133-9c62-17940a40a383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a16d1d62-6621-503c-b0f9-bb715a8e1719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467712} :answer-field/id #uuid "5635e07f-ff2a-5127-b631-682d05273e69" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "302cc8e5-06fe-55a0-88f7-cec7955d38ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467714} {:answer/id #uuid "6eded924-e650-5770-8da5-7d37948d90ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "302cc8e5-06fe-55a0-88f7-cec7955d38ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467714} :answer-field/id #uuid "4603a9a6-bdb5-51e4-b71c-7872c6351545" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7bb9654d-ae6a-57d3-8c11-b8ef9be232d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65009" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** ${e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- **III.** $3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)={e}^{x},b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n3{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+4{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $4{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "101e0c22-fbb4-5865-af5f-d669e2488d09" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Linear ODEs Using the Superposition Principle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e3999b2-cf3e-53ba-b81a-57a1167c43cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467716} {:answer/id #uuid "e76b57b4-95b4-56db-80ee-bc842c04362e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e3999b2-cf3e-53ba-b81a-57a1167c43cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467716} :answer-field/id #uuid "520b20a9-67a9-510c-8a4a-bf10f927a343" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ba558e-45ea-593a-af35-72261d300bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467718} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ab3a22-dcda-5034-a911-7a04245aaa46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8ab3a22-dcda-5034-a911-7a04245aaa46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467719} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d2cd27b-8211-54d2-9058-e0c068b1afab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ae1854-407d-5cdf-9e7f-245569682d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467720} {:answer/id #uuid "711403d4-4ed8-57e7-8ea2-e5ed05de59dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15ae1854-407d-5cdf-9e7f-245569682d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467720} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ad8c85-9200-5cf3-89f3-a6b9e7622899" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7815e919-91eb-5d8d-8ac9-3683413b2268" :question/math-academy-id "q-65110" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ are solutions to the equation ${y}^{″}+4y=0,$ which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n- **I.** $y(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}$\n- **II.** $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n- **III.** $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "According to the superposition principle, if the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are solutions to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ are constants, then $y(x)={c}_{1}{y}_{1}(x)+{c}_{2}{y}_{2}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nWe're given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Therefore, the following function is also a solution:\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+{c}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}$ is **not** a solution of the given equation. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotient of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is a solution of the given equation. Here, ${c}_{1}=1,{c}_{2}=5.$\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is **not** a solution of the given equation because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is not a solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba108ea-f332-5102-ab91-06fceec4d251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70a785c2-393a-5a94-bf91-ca5ecd6971b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467722} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d3662e-e09c-5f64-98c3-e20f9b22d088" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9529cf39-39ef-5312-a424-5a724c472342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467724} {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb84cc54-6743-5846-8d91-94b5fc81de0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467725} :answer-field/id #uuid "211c78a3-c7f3-5811-864c-a8d524c6218e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "269da86c-2941-58e2-a59d-268c780b46cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467726} {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204e2406-d430-5f85-b6af-e843171fc96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467727} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b3e117-4a2a-5afd-8320-ffa1d5324c25" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75bb764-05ea-55ac-922e-cca49efb6283" :question/math-academy-id "q-65821" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(0,-2\\pi )$\n- **II.** $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$\n- **III.** $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(0,-2\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-2\\pi ,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-2\\pi $ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,-2\\pi )$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8f2dda-cd81-5f6e-b768-a55c41ebc669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467728} {:answer/id #uuid "9734881e-341a-559d-9cd7-c83cf09900eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac8f2dda-cd81-5f6e-b768-a55c41ebc669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467728} :answer-field/id #uuid "25c993c6-73fa-53e6-afa4-9f57d2191ec9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1654988-d136-57e1-a888-8194db71b8d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467730} {:answer/id #uuid "23f8c642-a604-5c37-b052-b6e27965df40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1654988-d136-57e1-a888-8194db71b8d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "fa