ef 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467829} :answer-field/id #uuid "b885eb24-7891-5fc2-aedf-cfd5ba562b29" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b495bf5-5746-5288-a51e-cecce774eb37" :question/math-academy-id "q-70770" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n- **I.** $(-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$\n- **II.** $(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\n- **III.** $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},-\\frac{1}{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range.   $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{5\\pi }{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110587 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b834b64-9679-56c2-b5e9-ee26a54b5e13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a2d9a9-577b-5444-9d1c-92bf0a7facff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467830} {:answer/id #uuid "1eb1cc8e-f502-5f32-9bac-9ac87104593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb1cc8e-f502-5f32-9bac-9ac87104593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467831} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dc6e9d1-002a-50a3-a1d6-0ec8dcb2822d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac0f876-2044-5dca-a2b2-310d5490c170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467832} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b6825a-d045-54b6-8a0f-5d3a523bf157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b6825a-d045-54b6-8a0f-