:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0514df20-5bca-51ca-8efc-b76c2c3044a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467853} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a2ff425-5344-55a6-a715-3662f57b95c1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468647}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94a6f8a-60a9-5806-9e18-4814d39c5835" :question/math-academy-id "q-71395" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=1$ gives a line\n- **II.** $c=2$ gives a hyperbola\n- **III.** $c=0$ gives two lines" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=1,$ which is not a line.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=4,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=\\pm \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2}},$ which consists of two lines.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01f57d9-5382-51fc-bab4-ffea738f1ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467854} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b404fe-5087-57bf-b263-c61589eb6cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01f57d9-5382-51fc-bab4-ffea738f1ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467854} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e01aee-b504-51ec-a835-86adeb5908ec" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468648} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7303305-82d7-590b-bd4e-1a4e70d19cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467856} {:answer/id #uuid "95ef83b9-f720-5a51-bbca-96fc09dbbf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ef83b9-f720-5a51-bbca-96fc09dbbf9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467857} :answer-field/id #uuid "bac3a257-72fb-5727-a2e2-607cc6489f5b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68c2fa7d-c1fb-55e0-9e76-3d220bf461d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467858} {:answer/id #uuid "1e4ddb26-d234-57e3-82d0-9980a51f2163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68c2fa7d-c1fb-55e0-9e76-3d220bf461d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467858} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d88f0f-e223-519e-a68d-b17bad084659" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1e22680-b6e5-5705-939d-f4a384a3db7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71791" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n- **I.** $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$\n- **II.** $[-1,1]$\n- **III.** $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[-1,1]$ is closed. The boundary points are $-1$, and $1.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $(3,5)\\cup [2,3)$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup (7,10]$ has a boundary point $0$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15e435d9-0d0c-57a7-b750-2fe6e91de38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467860} {:answer/id #uuid "124179ee-ec18-565c-8e41-d6a38b6648d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "124179ee-ec18-565c-8e41-d6a38b6648d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467861} :answer-field/id #uuid "d32fbe7a-e8bf-58e8-87a2-4469f95dadcb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b04679a-cdc2-503e-9e56-5f54340d850e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467862} {:answer/id #uuid "560bd919-6c05-51e5-be0a-1e97bf0f2100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b04679a-cdc2-503e-9e56-5f54340d850e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467862} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f59797d-12b2-53fc-b302-f28e7b141f34" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468652} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4bc2964-0554-5078-acf3-fb9a8ebdd1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467864} {:answer/id #uuid "d53b6194-061b-5e9a-bb9a-e89015f4c765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4bc2964-0554-5078-acf3-fb9a8ebdd1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467864} :answer-field/id #uuid "95be5ba9-d56c-5766-a506-02a900406ee5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20e43566-ea3c-59ee-a80b-84f1522c9eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-71798" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-\\infty ,-2)$\n\nII. $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$\n\nIII. $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-\\infty ,-2)$ is open. The boundary point of the set is $-2$ and it does not lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $(0,2]\\cup [7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $2$, $7$, and $9$, and the points $2$, $7$, and $9$ lies in the set.\n\n- $[-5,-1]\\cup (2,4)$ has four boundary points $-5$, $-1$, $2$, and $4$, and the points $-5$ and $-1$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d97f9b1-cd02-5db7-b2bc-f5cc82fd1fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467866} {:answer/id #uuid "16d6c84b-080a-524c-9f25-2308e8f31793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d97f9b1-cd02-5db7-b2bc-f5cc82fd1fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467866} :answer-field/id #uuid "262aa83b-bc34-5f27-a72e-d2195e3fc4a0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d94692c-4b2e-5401-bcba-d9bf9366009a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467868} {:answer/id #uuid "36a247b0-63d5-509e-a764-58bd560bdecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d94692c-4b2e-5401-bcba-d9bf9366009a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467868} :answer-field/id #uuid "28132271-bfa7-578b-9764-11df14aa48f4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0314ff64-20a7-5d2f-9389-7ffebc54fbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467870} {:answer/id #uuid "24c4ed0a-4ee8-526a-8e67-5e5ac60e0f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24c4ed0a-4ee8-526a-8e67-5e5ac60e0f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467871} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a82fe14-d8d7-504c-aa26-fa21ff5593ce" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be4bb9a2-432f-5bf7-aa6c-466035df5777" :question/math-academy-id "q-71802" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n- **I.** $[-7,1]$\n- **II.** $(-1,3]\\cup [4,5)$\n- **III.** $(-5,-1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-5,-1)$ is open. The boundary points are $-5$, and $-1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $[-7,1]$ has two boundary points $-7$, and $1$, and both of them lie in the set.\n\n- $(-1,3]\\cup [4,5)$ has four boundary points $-1$, $3$, $4$, and $5$, and the points $3$ and $4$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0facf7b-b440-550d-a4f0-7ff4c1c70086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467872} {:answer/id #uuid "923dab7f-47a4-5a3e-98eb-2cce0c04c4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "923dab7f-47a4-5a3e-98eb-2cce0c04c4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467873} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b347d78-d76c-546b-9764-685fc8bce910" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468657} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a04b7c-fb3d-5af9-ac13-b910623c1d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467874} {:answer/id #uuid "22c1d005-4f0b-5972-a387-b7ee798fd110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22a04b7c-fb3d-5af9-ac13-b910623c1d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6202c391-be1c-57b1-848b-195b5e71c27f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468658} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5074ee4-5219-56ad-b17c-122d6139dd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467876} {:answer/id #uuid "8b927c21-a2f7-54c8-a565-a983c6bbb42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b927c21-a2f7-54c8-a565-a983c6bbb42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467877} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c56bb76-335e-5a28-aec0-4d8270bf15ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1615097-eb1e-5984-b134-50e4277f6126" :question/math-academy-id "q-71814" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }x<y<{x}^{2},\\,1<x\\le 2\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2<y<x\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<9\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,2).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b5c97d8-b6b9-59d5-9e48-f02e00576bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467878} {:answer/id #uuid "b70b7d57-44be-598c-81f7-72a6992ce643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b5c97d8-b6b9-59d5-9e48-f02e00576bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467878} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e6bbccd-f9e1-5e48-a3e5-91c54d7aa28d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/iden