\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }1\\le x<3,\\,2<y\\le 4}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }2{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}<6}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,4).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *open *since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "440337ae-e75b-5e2e-af72-f244faaa1466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467884} {:answer/id #uuid "84120805-e8ea-59f8-8390-7f0edacbe1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84120805-e8ea-59f8-8390-7f0edacbe1f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467885} :answer-field/id #uuid "df2c75d9-b4ef-5178-ba10-74ba6baa1d94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468663} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afd201de-1dae-5ce1-9c43-571f88d6eff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467886} {:answer/id #uuid "bb427474-e6dd-5ecd-9ad5-db3243527e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd201de-1dae-5ce1-9c43-571f88d6eff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467886} :answer-field/id #uuid "a36383fc-6ca1-5ff1-8d63-ce4e0dfeba1b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "703aafea-bae6-565a-8269-49fb586e4b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467888} {:answer/id #uuid "e33ef251-1fda-59d8-80c6-61a0acfd6e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e33ef251-1fda-59d8-80c6-61a0acfd6e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467889} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b47c5fa-a986-5f5a-a620-2cf86189fd7c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef298213-bf03-538b-9273-2913d7465266" :question/math-academy-id "q-71819" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 2\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<{y}^{2}<4\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x<1,\\,{y}^{2}<4\\}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,\\sqrt{2}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c4606f-5c57-58fd-9b55-f0f565399e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467890} {:answer/id #uuid "839ad9eb-979f-5d6a-9652-cf932de67c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c4606f-5c57-58fd-9b55-f0f565399e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467890} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dbd3ff-e733-5ef8-8e2a-4b6a3ed482cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d16d0d-a7d6-5c86-a450-48bdb56fa68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467892} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c7da8b-4115-5fbe-a39e-f59aa55b52dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c7da8b-4115-5fbe-a39e-f59aa55b52dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467893} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3b918c5-6776-5588-87a5-8e477039d79d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "038d16c2-35c1-5438-83bc-59c1edc2bf77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467894} {:answer/id #uuid "12c9ca01-2f6e-5d33-b261-04041c5b6a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "038d16c2-35c1-5438-83bc-59c1edc2bf77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467894} :answer-field/id #uuid "b81e4c73-2f9e-5840-a8ed-1a1cab4f8bc5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d61f9b2d-e5ea-58f1-be0f-837958c85bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71820" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\,1<y\\le 4}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 9}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,4).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (the corresponding inequality is not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd7bbbf-6e0c-51c5-a9fa-fc0f2bf1d945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467896} {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c58e8001-ca94-52dc-9ac3-efcb68b4cfa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467897} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afb67d1-8168-5df5-930f-8190b07edc62" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6fa4bf8-f217-5274-8dab-28c162bb278d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467898} {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f93fd016-1442-53ad-8597-12bc1e59568b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467899} :answer-field/id #uuid "a00bd3e1-111e-5780-871b-467da013e81a" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} {:answer/id #uuid "906cb48c-7d29-5136-a248-2c29457a1fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f78fc2c-5319-559a-b65c-0b1064d9bbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467900} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4c5cafc-4559-5564-a3f4-1bb51c7edb62" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6118feb2-c751-599a-b3b9-c8c760c49b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71934" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}15 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $R$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(R)=5\\cdot 4-10\\cdot 2=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(R)=0,$ we conclude that $R$ is not invertible.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $T$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $S$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04e9358-9109-5802-a83d-c003136f6776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467902} {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "711d5a0b-0232-5cb7-8a88-a13f69141094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467903} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b39826b-4d43-597b-b35d-5dd3a91ceaf8" :answer-field/key "X" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6c71b-66a8-52d7-88ab-87e3a0607923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af6e952f-1b3d-5415-9986-1f855a35a9dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f838e05-1a03-57ee-8f9c-10a9e960bcdd" :answer-field/key "Y" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62048c-e540-5983-8cbf-aabcf18ff59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e98450e-f707-5f45-880a-72823035ac85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2386ffd6-0069-5a17-ae65-0bf5f760c977" :answer-field/key "Z" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f09c20fa-fbe3-5a9f-8218-d2a4dd2af13c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fdb0af4-bec9-5365-971f-ab546cd82d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467908} {:answer/id #uuid "d80b7404-e065-5db5-bcce-93cc1aebc4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fdb0af4-bec9-5365-971f-ab546cd82d92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467908} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f8ce43-df76-5fc6-89d1-78a9a1e48f97" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3564aa95-c89d-5d78-b74c-425d2b171124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467910} {:answer/id #uuid "18c2174c-460e-5990-bc37-38b8de7a5f0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3564aa95-c89d-5d78-b74c-425d2b171124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467910} :answer-field/id #uuid "2506e38a-e7c8-5102-ae2e-637f98ec3c36" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8e879d1-636a-58da-87a1-9d0e2524a6d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467912} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9a4911-e986-55a6-a8fd-43e12eed4d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b9a4911-e986-55a6-a8fd-43e12eed4d2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467913} :answer-field/id #uuid "046d1d39-39e9-58b5-8e61-b97eee9247b1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2073d8ee-8ecd-594e-9fd2-e836c959a0b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-72130" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}.$\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $1$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7b78cd2-bfb7-5330-aa6f-f7ce269e6b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467914} {:answer/id #uuid "27a8076d-8705-5d50-a53c-95dab2e496b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a8076d-8705-5d50-a53c-95dab2e496b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467915} :answer-field/id #uuid "d454bd2e-767a-5f21-944b-ed804dfff5fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcc390e-ef7a-55fd-9a12-5d600f7acf1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467916} {:answer/id #uuid "d2164cbf-cf1d-578d-80b9-b112dd5bfb34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2164cbf-cf1d-578d-80b9-b112dd5bfb34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467917} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce312647-eb92-5dce-aa4c-9426b435bac5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cebe6bcc-6e83-516f-a0d5-c7fdae04f696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467918} {:answer/id #uuid "9baf9625-6765-5ea4-92b5-cb80c7acefbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cebe6bcc-6e83-516f-a0d5-c7fdae04f696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467918} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a3b488-fd9e-5da4-9e1a-9d233a047903" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4009c26-3316-54ec-b0bf-1d56ecb8b0b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72175" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28e2c148-6ee6-5f8c-9b2b-442fe96cf085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467920} {:answer/id #uuid "90143807-a74a-57ee-aa16-a1ee057a16c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90143807-a74a-57ee-aa16-a1ee057a16c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467921} :answer-field/id #uuid "2de9075c-99a1-540e-b78d-991060565cb7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468681} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8488a4b-f9b2-5a2f-aeff-132fefe2716f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467922} {:answer/id #uuid "1a62f2dd-5c52-5ce6-8102-f840944d8ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a62f2dd-5c52-5ce6-8102-f840944d8ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467923} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5389031-03cb-5727-b801-66a146d9f193" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25b7c356-4e59-589f-9d6a-565ed0873aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467924} {:answer/id #uuid "58cf1eb8-5878-59da-b070-f3f00fcdcb15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25b7c356-4e59-589f-9d6a-565ed0873aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467924} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb366d99-7744-5bfb-8897-cc8aae3154da" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bcd8034-22f3-5298-b8d3-b69cdcbc84fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-72185" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/09/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cb3d1e7-cf6a-54b2-a095-b9fdc68a8d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467926} {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab149b0-2702-528d-b56e-23d4232647f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467927} :answer-field/id #uuid "368ddd66-9d80-586f-9e2a-9ab70f075343" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} {:answer/id #uuid "7d445f31-2d12-5062-a2a4-99e2b64c0491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ea3c229-904d-5a2f-8d07-a00dada077bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467928} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edea166-3bfd-535f-b98e-b624be2d49a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} {:answer/id #uuid "1541c926-bd73-5e47-854d-d4e15738f59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94e95bb-c951-576f-aa60-7b79a87fb894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467930} :answer-field/id #uuid "88bc4663-71c0-5111-9c92-a5bd0ddc37dc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f581ab20-43e5-59a8-ac58-914378a7361e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72186" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/76/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4ef645-0e9e-59ca-9ead-4e534938e7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93784bc3-b560-52b9-a35d-2ec831b381f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467932} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae03209-445f-57ef-a7d8-bf499239612a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} {:answer/id #uuid "652141fa-413d-505f-be84-3dff8c027c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea766b7-5902-5718-9a79-ebd9d7790d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467934} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1a093da-8121-5419-baa0-42398a34c5c0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38c7e8b2-4b4c-577e-a27a-0aa07ff9fbc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467936} {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "482c64c9-5eab-5414-829d-60978c25b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7660e82-ac96-5396-b514-daa03b2886a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b03842bf-e94f-5526-903d-de5a2a3bccca" :question/math-academy-id "q-72187" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/28/28290c5530efd27a979f4284481ca7e0384342d7d426dde0ab36894a0d77a166.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/30/3007cffb725faee44d2a06ad077eec630791b1a94c373a323f62d0d721c87207.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/38/383f88668435556d3a856cf852caf548b1f1bf3a90d50f9d85d7968188984804.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23b28d03-cd57-5d78-8671-e5c1d46ed665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467938} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed66caf-fe28-584a-83bf-1f36896c365e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23b28d03-cd57-5d78-8671-e5c1d46ed665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467938} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd09d61-c1f0-556d-8c4e-0dd624a70cf5" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b617e07-2740-58b3-b6a5-d9472e257ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467940} {:answer/id #uuid "b4308405-a8a5-56c9-af60-06c16d1d14d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4308405-a8a5-56c9-af60-06c16d1d14d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467941} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee97b22-001a-5361-9e3b-138ef357939a" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94af9650-c777-5740-9917-82f863d1fd15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467942} {:answer/id #uuid "3369f3e3-6e3d-5e75-b2a8-d84fac360cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3369f3e3-6e3d-5e75-b2a8-d84fac360cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d389fe9-b790-5945-910d-6661d44a7238" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ddf8ccb-f483-5bbe-8662-ef5250ea89a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72489" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aad04b9e-e1c0-5bb1-8988-f13ae2b12a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467944} {:answer/id #uuid "182256c0-eed4-5308-8899-646442169606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aad04b9e-e1c0-5bb1-8988-f13ae2b12a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467944} :answer-field/id #uuid "e337cd9d-13a4-5dac-9234-3d41da87d9a0" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0777136a-d863-5438-b95f-bc866c333a22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467946} {:answer/id #uuid "96cecc84-650b-5579-bf1d-d6d830e791b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96cecc84-650b-5579-bf1d-d6d830e791b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467947} :answer-field/id #uuid "a790397a-6735-5a19-8785-3d13a0ca79b8" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72991cce-897b-580a-82d9-a6ea9e4374ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467948} {:answer/id #uuid "44145af0-fb61-51cd-b673-1a7fef08d8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72991cce-897b-580a-82d9-a6ea9e4374ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467948} :answer-field/id #uuid "05c578b4-fa57-5327-837b-e40c8423b3ba" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "937eaf0d-76e6-56ec-a651-23458856322a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72498" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$  is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} {:answer/id #uuid "5df8e8f3-9308-5944-af31-4d14c71a9d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} :answer-field/id #uuid "00781771-aeb9-5835-884e-fa3c06c40e7e" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ee2b9e-ef1d-59cf-bd65-2b7d6a2bf08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467952} {:answer/id #uuid "d81beee0-f7cd-5ee1-a153-c2609ec12ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81beee0-f7cd-5ee1-a153-c2609ec12ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953} :answer-field/id #uuid "625436a2-9099-57c0-a144-3cefd737c380" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a341d39f-fed1-52da-a5bf-5551842652b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467954} {:answer/id #uuid "5061ada4-2851-5b12-9dcc-a52396a7b645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5061ada4-2851-5b12-9dcc-a52396a7b645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955} :answer-field/id #uuid "4691ceca-21a9-5d3f-be55-1f587cc36770" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f7d9000-6b1e-59bb-84e6-86f972afc228" :question/math-academy-id "q-72570" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$  is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871c0b9a-48a3-59d8-9e1f-f4475d4555bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db