e7192f0-0469-5c77-92a1-060194834d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-73482" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+1}}?$   \n- **I.** $[-1,0]$\n- **II.** $[1,10]$\n- **III.** $(-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,0]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=-1.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,10]$ is  closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,10].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval  $(-1,0)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2fb7032-76c6-5840-a4b3-75b3bca0c64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468022} {:answer/id #uuid "7da58ced-39e0-5469-8345-6d5c5c71fd19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2fb7032-76c6-5840-a4b3-75b3bca0c64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468022} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5aeadf-4637-56d4-8985-6b916361fe7c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ide