ulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd25b025-461f-556b-97f3-6071c19d59d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-75595" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,$ ${R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1},\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 2x2 