\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3917c546-1a71-5b69-95fa-031bd8a95f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468148} {:answer/id #uuid "685efbb1-a98a-5e24-81fb-c69c96152f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685efbb1-a98a-5e24-81fb-c69c96152f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468149} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4d8e60-f36f-5898-86ce-56958409039b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "799189fe-d9b2-592f-8d4d-7c1f35029fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468150} {:answer/id #uuid "4b25fdd6-dd1d-55bd-b563-27dbc04b5ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "799189fe-d9b2-592f-8d4d-7c1f35029fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468150} :answer-field/id #uuid "24d36265-d1fc-567a-8fcc-21fe29ff2d57" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c73bf89d-de06-5c8f-ac60-6e163bb23230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468152} {:answer/id #uuid "0777f273-c934-5fa7-a08b-0aa490e67340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c73bf89d-de06-5c8f-ac60-6e163bb23230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468152} :answer-field/id #uuid "22390857-93d9-508c-9a5a-4191c39a0625" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f25df3d-4b0c-5b67-901d-8d878d2769ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-75655" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n- **III.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 12{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bafe8fd-72d8-57d1-bc5f-2d080ed75be6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468154} {:answer/id #uuid "85d07ff4-4f7d-5633-83c1-35a840fa221c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604549